WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.445 --> 00:00:15.234
On Christmas morning, the March sisters awoke early because they wanted to surprise Mother with their gifts.

2
00:00:16.895 --> 00:00:20.998
Jo reached under the bed and pulled out a wooden box where the gifts for Mother were hidden.

3
00:00:21.018 --> 00:00:25.181
"I hope Mother likes this," said Jo.

4
00:00:26.122 --> 00:00:28.444
She held up a wrapped parcel close to her heart.

5
00:00:29.068 --> 00:00:31.129
Jo had penned a poem just for Mother.

6
00:00:32.149 --> 00:00:35.871
Beth fingered her gift to Mother: two handkerchiefs with daisies.

7
00:00:36.811 --> 00:00:38.372
She had spent all night making them.

8
00:00:39.352 --> 00:00:44.475
Although some of the daisies looked like uneven yellow spots, Beth hoped Mother would love them.

9
00:00:44.495 --> 00:00:47.796
"Smell how lovely that is."

10
00:00:48.396 --> 00:00:50.777
Amy pressed a small box under Meg's nose.

11
00:00:50.797 --> 00:00:53.399
"Did you get lavender?

12
00:00:53.859 --> 00:00:56.540
It's Mother's favorite," Meg said knowingly.

13
00:00:57.616 --> 00:01:00.718
Amy had used her savings to buy a bottle of cologne for Mother.

14
00:01:00.738 --> 00:01:07.183
"Of course it's lavender, though my personal preference is roses," said Amy.

15
00:01:07.203 --> 00:01:09.845
"Meg, where is your gift?"

16
00:01:10.305 --> 00:01:12.546
Jo lifted the wooden box and shook it hard.

17
00:01:12.566 --> 00:01:15.268
"Oh, I have it here," said Meg.

18
00:01:16.049 --> 00:01:19.731
From her pocket she pulled out a bundle wrapped in a silk handkerchief.

19
00:01:20.812 --> 00:01:23.294
Inside was a pair of white silk gloves.

20
00:01:24.655 --> 00:01:26.236
Jo squeezed Meg's hand.

21
00:01:27.196 --> 00:01:31.457
She knew that Meg had saved her hard earned money to purchase those special gloves.

22
00:01:31.477 --> 00:01:38.339
"They will fit Mother's hands perfectly," Meg said as she lovingly placed them inside the box.

23
00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:43.020
The girls crept quietly downstairs to the living room.

24
00:01:44.221 --> 00:01:49.062
Mother usually reclined in her chair sipping her coffee before the girls scurried in for breakfast.

25
00:01:49.802 --> 00:01:55.324
So, in order to surprise her, the girls tiptoed across the hall and stood quietly outside the living

26
00:01:55.344 --> 00:01:55.944
room entrance.

27
00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:58.470
Amy had a fit of giggles.

28
00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:03.093
"Shh!" Jo hissed at her.

29
00:02:03.113 --> 00:02:06.636
"Girls, on the count of three," Meg whispered.

30
00:02:06.656 --> 00:02:10.318
"One, two THREE!"

31
00:02:11.139 --> 00:02:16.043
The girls flew into the room and shouted simultaneously: "Surprise, Mother!

32
00:02:16.163 --> 00:02:22.908
Merry—!" But before they could finish their greeting, the girls noticed Mother's chair was unoccupied.

33
00:02:24.156 --> 00:02:27.237
Instead Hannah had just strolled in with a tray full of cakes.

34
00:02:27.257 --> 00:02:32.678
"Ah!" Hannah screamed as she almost flipped the tray over.

35
00:02:33.559 --> 00:02:35.979
Meg ran over to help their beloved housekeeper.

36
00:02:35.999 --> 00:02:39.060
"Oh, girls!"

37
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:44.101
Amy clasped her hands, her eyes growing big as she looked at the dining room table.

38
00:02:45.082 --> 00:02:47.322
The table was covered with heaps of food.

39
00:02:48.323 --> 00:02:53.544
There were sausages, eggs, fresh juice and butter, and cakes adorned each corner.

40
00:02:55.872 --> 00:03:02.737
"Your Ma wanted to surprise you girls with a Christmas feast," said Hannah, still clutching her chest and

41
00:03:02.837 --> 00:03:03.757
breathing deeply.

42
00:03:05.078 --> 00:03:08.140
The girls were so touched by their mother's loving act.

43
00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.202
"But where is she?"

44
00:03:10.622 --> 00:03:11.082
asked Jo.

45
00:03:11.763 --> 00:03:15.085
Before Hannah could answer, Mother walked in through the front door.

46
00:03:15.105 --> 00:03:18.547
"Good morning, my darling girls!"

47
00:03:19.368 --> 00:03:22.089
Mother opened her arms wide to embrace her daughters.

48
00:03:22.109 --> 00:03:25.652
"Where did you go, Mother?"

49
00:03:26.036 --> 00:03:26.637
Meg asked.

50
00:03:27.597 --> 00:03:30.079
"I went to see the Hummels," replied Mother.

51
00:03:30.899 --> 00:03:34.242
The Hummels were a very poor family with many small children.

52
00:03:35.042 --> 00:03:40.726
Mr. Hummel had been drafted into the army, leaving his pregnant wife and six small children to fend

53
00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:41.406
for themselves.

54
00:03:42.547 --> 00:03:48.571
Since Mother worked as a volunteer to help unfortunate people in the community, she knew the Hummels' situation

55
00:03:48.731 --> 00:03:49.272
very well.

56
00:03:49.292 --> 00:03:51.793
"How are the children?"

57
00:03:52.314 --> 00:03:53.254
asked Beth gently.

58
00:03:53.274 --> 00:03:57.269
"Not very good, I'm afraid," Mother answered gravely.

59
00:03:57.289 --> 00:04:00.652
"They have no heating or food."

60
00:04:01.533 --> 00:04:04.576
Her voice trailed off as she looked at the feast on the table.

61
00:04:05.357 --> 00:04:10.401
The girls knew what Mother was thinking, but except for Beth, the other girls were reluctant to part

62
00:04:10.441 --> 00:04:11.502
with their Christmas meal.

63
00:04:12.944 --> 00:04:15.926
Meg reasoned to herself: "We don't get any gifts.

64
00:04:16.987 --> 00:04:19.370
We should at least get a decent Christmas meal."

65
00:04:20.651 --> 00:04:23.697
Jo was thinking: "I'm starving!

66
00:04:23.917 --> 00:04:26.278
And those sausages look so appetizing!"

67
00:04:27.238 --> 00:04:33.201
Amy contemplated: "Maybe we can eat first then give the rest away to the Hummels."

68
00:04:34.281 --> 00:04:37.282
Mother smiled at them as if she could discern their very thoughts.

69
00:04:38.042 --> 00:04:42.984
But she said kindly: "I just want to say that this meal is a gift from me and

70
00:04:43.044 --> 00:04:43.905
Hannah to you.

71
00:04:44.545 --> 00:04:47.826
However you want to use your gift is entirely up to you.

72
00:04:48.727 --> 00:04:51.728
I will love and respect you whatever you decide."

73
00:04:52.848 --> 00:04:53.869
Meg spoke first.

74
00:04:54.369 --> 00:04:59.173
"Mother, the girls and I would be honored if the Hummels could enjoy this lovely meal."

75
00:05:01.494 --> 00:05:03.236
Jo and Beth nodded in agreement.

76
00:05:04.376 --> 00:05:06.798
A moment or two later, Amy nodded too.

77
00:05:06.818 --> 00:05:12.202
"My girls, I am so proud of you," Mother said.

78
00:05:12.222 --> 00:05:16.805
"Let's all go together to visit the Hummels," suggested Beth.

79
00:05:17.626 --> 00:05:20.528
So the girls sprinted upstairs to change their clothes.

80
00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.881
Within a few minutes, the food was all wrapped up and ready to go.

81
00:05:25.742 --> 00:05:28.463
The girls got into their boots and coats and ventured out.

82
00:05:30.124 --> 00:05:32.705
Each of them carried large baskets filled with food.

83
00:05:33.545 --> 00:05:37.807
As the Hummels did not have any heating, Jo hauled a sack of wood as well.

84
00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:41.268
None of the girls felt regret or resentment.

85
00:05:42.209 --> 00:05:46.210
Deep in their hearts, they knew the Hummels would relish the meal much more than they would.

86
00:05:47.611 --> 00:05:51.484
As they passed the old mansion next to their house, Jo happened to look up.

87
00:05:52.445 --> 00:05:57.006
From the third floor, a dark-haired boy peered down at them as they trudged along.

88
00:05:58.207 --> 00:05:59.787
"Look! There's old Mr.

89
00:05:59.827 --> 00:06:01.047
Laurence's grandson!"

90
00:06:01.348 --> 00:06:02.768
Jo called out to her sisters.

91
00:06:02.788 --> 00:06:05.349
"Jo!" reprimanded Meg.

92
00:06:05.889 --> 00:06:07.149
"Stop staring at him.

93
00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:10.470
It isn't proper for a young girl to stare at a boy!"

94
00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:16.192
"Don't be such a granny, Meg," snorted Jo.

95
00:06:16.212 --> 00:06:20.554
Since both her hands were full, she lifted up her foot and wiggled it at him as an

96
00:06:20.614 --> 00:06:21.694
alternative to waving.

97
00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:24.676
"Jo! You're so shameless!"

98
00:06:25.016 --> 00:06:25.996
said Amy in rebuke.

99
00:06:27.237 --> 00:06:31.139
From the window the boy also lifted his foot and wiggled it at Jo.

100
00:06:31.919 --> 00:06:33.880
Jo let out a loud, hearty laugh.

101
00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:40.303
No words could describe how grateful the Hummel family was for the generous gift.

102
00:06:41.103 --> 00:06:45.649
Jo expertly got a fire going in no time while Meg and Amy set up the table and

103
00:06:45.729 --> 00:06:46.510
filled it with food.

104
00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.531
Beth and Mother took care of the sick children.

105
00:06:49.551 --> 00:06:54.194
"Did you see how happy those children were?"

106
00:06:54.654 --> 00:06:58.797
Amy said, as the girls walked back home, her footsteps light and perky.

107
00:06:58.817 --> 00:07:03.019
"Mrs. Hummel could not stop crying," remarked Jo.

108
00:07:03.039 --> 00:07:05.521
"I felt so sorry for her."

109
00:07:05.541 --> 00:07:07.422
"Hopefully Mr.

110
00:07:07.462 --> 00:07:10.644
Hummel will be able to return home soon," said Mother.

111
00:07:11.508 --> 00:07:14.590
Silently, all the girls prayed for their father to do the same.

112
00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:19.492
As the girls got nearer to their house, something made them stop.

113
00:07:19.512 --> 00:07:21.713
"Is that our house?"

114
00:07:22.153 --> 00:07:22.673
asked Amy.

115
00:07:22.693 --> 00:07:28.096
"Well, I think so, but it looks different somehow," replied Meg.

116
00:07:28.756 --> 00:07:32.258
There was a warm glow to the house as if each room was emitting heat.

117
00:07:32.278 --> 00:07:34.959
"What if the house is on fire?"

118
00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:35.980
Jo shouted.

119
00:07:37.064 --> 00:07:41.607
She tore across the field, her hair flying out of its bun, and threw open the door.

120
00:07:43.108 --> 00:07:44.309
What a sight to behold!

121
00:07:44.909 --> 00:07:49.533
The entire house was cozily warm, a fire burning brightly in each fireplace.

122
00:07:50.453 --> 00:07:54.616
The bare dining room table was once again crowded with all sorts of delights.

123
00:07:54.636 --> 00:07:57.938
"Hannah! What is this?"

124
00:07:58.378 --> 00:07:59.639
Mother demanded to know.

125
00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:06.304
Choking back tears, Hannah could produce no reply but simply pointed to the mansion next door.

126
00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:08.941
"You mean Mr.

127
00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:10.222
Laurence sent this?"

128
00:08:10.682 --> 00:08:11.162
asked Mother.

129
00:08:12.043 --> 00:08:15.185
Hannah nodded, overcome by a fresh wave of tears.

130
00:08:15.205 --> 00:08:17.346
"Here's a card!"

131
00:08:17.706 --> 00:08:21.889
Jo waved a small piece of paper in the air: Dear Mrs.

132
00:08:21.969 --> 00:08:28.213
March and all her lovely daughters, Jo read: My grandson and I would like to give a gift

133
00:08:28.253 --> 00:08:30.754
to you as you so generously give to others.

134
00:08:31.555 --> 00:08:32.195
Your neighbor, Mr.

135
00:08:34.476 --> 00:08:37.878
Laurence. The girls all grabbed hands and started to dance around the table.

136
00:08:38.538 --> 00:08:40.640
Never had they been so surprised.

137
00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:43.861
"You see, girls," Mother said happily.

138
00:08:43.881 --> 00:08:47.804
"When you think of others, others are also thinking of you."
